---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import Command from '../components/Command.astro';
import Workbench from '../components/Workbench.astro';
import { path, github } from '../lib/links';
const steps = [
  { number: '01', title: 'Investigate in Plan mode', mode: 'PLAN', text: 'Read and search the codebase with workspace mutations disabled. The result is a reviewable plan.', key: 'Shift + Tab', detail: 'Switch between Plan and Build' },
  { number: '02', title: 'Edit and run commands', mode: 'BUILD', text: 'Allow file edits and shell commands. Tool calls and command results appear in the timeline.', key: 'Ctrl + W', detail: 'Open the working set' },
  { number: '03', title: 'Review the changes', mode: 'INSPECT', text: 'Inspect changed files, diffs, test output, and tracked processes before ending the session.', key: 'Ctrl + F', detail: 'Explore workspace files' },
];
---
<Site title="zarlcode — Terminal coding agent with plan and build modes" description="Use zarlcode to inspect a codebase, edit files, run commands, and review diffs from a terminal interface.">
  <section class="hero container" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="hero-topline"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> ZARLCODE / TERMINAL CODING AGENT</p><span class="eyebrow hero-aside">OPEN SOURCE / GO</span></div>
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <h1 id="hero-title">Plan, run, and review coding tasks <span class="accent">in the terminal.</span></h1>
      <div class="hero-copy"><p class="lead">A model conversation, workspace tools, and a diff viewer in one terminal interface.</p><p>Use read-only Plan mode to investigate a task. Switch to Build to edit files and run commands. Tool calls, results, and changes remain available for review in the session.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="#install">Install zarlcode <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="#workflow">View the workflow <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div><div class="hero-footnote"><span>SQLite sessions</span><span>Hosted and local providers</span><span>MIT licensed</span></div></div>
    </div>
    <Workbench />
  </section>
  <div class="provider-strip"><div class="container provider-inner"><span class="eyebrow">SUPPORTED PROVIDERS AND ENDPOINTS</span><div class="provider-list"><span>Anthropic</span><span>OpenAI</span><span>Gemini</span><span>DeepSeek</span><span>Ollama</span><a href={path('zarlcode-providers/')}>View provider setup ↗</a></div></div></div>
  <section class="section container" id="workflow" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / SESSION WORKFLOW</p><h2 id="workflow-title">Use Plan mode, Build mode, and the inspection views.</h2></div><p>Start with read-only investigation, enable workspace changes when the plan is ready, then review the files and command output produced during the turn.</p></div>
    <div class="workflow-grid">{steps.map((step) => <article class="workflow-step"><div class="step-top"><span class="step-number">{step.number}</span><span class="eyebrow">{step.mode}</span></div><h3>{step.title}</h3><p>{step.text}</p><div class="key-note"><kbd>{step.key}</kbd><span>{step.detail}</span></div></article>)}</div>
    <a class="text-link section-link" href={path('zarlcode-workflow/')}>Walk through your first session <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </section>
  <section class="section control-section" aria-labelledby="control-title">
    <div class="container control-grid"><div class="control-heading"><p class="eyebrow">02 / SESSION REVIEW</p><h2 id="control-title">The interface records what the agent did.</h2><p>The timeline shows model output alongside tool calls and results. Separate views cover changed files, diffs, workspace files, and tracked processes.</p><a class="text-link" href={path('zarlcode-interface/')}>Read the interface guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="terminal-note" aria-hidden="true"><span>~/workspace</span><br /><span class="accent">❯</span> zarlcode<span class="cursor">_</span></div></div>
      <div class="feature-list">
        <article><span class="feature-symbol" aria-hidden="true">↳</span><div><h3>Timeline and working set</h3><p>The timeline contains model output, tool calls, and command results. The working set lists changed files, diffs, and background processes.</p><a href={path('zarlcode-interface/')}>Interface reference ↗</a></div></article>
        <article><span class="feature-symbol" aria-hidden="true">↺</span><div><h3>Local session storage</h3><p>Sessions are stored in local SQLite. Canonical transcripts are stored separately from the model context used for later requests.</p><a href={path('sessions-transcripts/')}>Session storage reference ↗</a></div></article>
        <article><span class="feature-symbol" aria-hidden="true">⇄</span><div><h3>Provider and model selection</h3><p>Select a hosted provider or configure a local OpenAI-compatible endpoint. Provider and model settings are available in the TUI.</p><a href={path('zarlcode-providers/')}>Provider configuration ↗</a></div></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section container" id="built-with-zkit" aria-labelledby="toolkit-title">
    <div class="toolkit-panel"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 / ZKIT</p><h2 id="toolkit-title">The agent runtime is available as Go packages.</h2><p><strong>zkit supplies the runner, tool interfaces, provider adapters, guardrails, and session infrastructure used by zarlcode.</strong> Applications can import the individual packages they need.</p><a class="button button-outline" href={path('toolkit/')}>View the zkit overview <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="stack-diagram" aria-label="A Go application composed from zkit runner, tools, and provider packages."><div class="stack-label eyebrow">PACKAGE COMPOSITION</div><div class="stack-app"><span>application</span><span class="muted">.go</span></div><div class="stack-connector" aria-hidden="true">↓</div><div class="stack-modules"><span>runner</span><span>tools</span><span>providers</span></div><div class="stack-foundation"><span class="accent">zkit</span><span>Go packages</span></div><p>Used by zarlcode and the SWE-bench evaluation driver.</p></div></div>
  </section>
  <section class="install-section" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-title"><div class="container install-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">04 / INSTALL</p><h2 id="install-title">Install and run zarlcode in a workspace.</h2><p>The first launch creates local configuration and opens provider setup in the TUI.</p><a class="text-link" href={path('zarlcode-onboarding/')}>Read the installation guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="install-card"><Command command="brew install zarldev/tap/zarlcode" label="01 / INSTALL WITH HOMEBREW" /><Command command="cd /path/to/your/workspace && zarlcode" label="02 / LAUNCH IN YOUR WORKSPACE" /><p class="install-help">Configure a provider in the TUI with <kbd>Ctrl + S</kbd>. Local models require a separately running model server.</p><div class="install-links"><a href={`${github}/releases`}>Release downloads ↗</a><a href={path('zarlcode/#install')}>Build from source ↗</a></div></div></div><div class="container safety-note"><span aria-hidden="true">↳</span><p>Sessions are stored locally. Hosted providers receive model requests. Build mode edits files and runs commands with the current user's privileges. <a href={path('zarlcode-safety/')}>Read the safety and access guide ↗</a></p></div></section>
</Site>
